Falsifies `package_archive::verification::a_parsed_package_reads_only_inside_itself`.

The defect: the table of contents is measured in entries rather than in bytes, dropping the
`* MEMBER_LEN`. The line still reads as "the header plus the table", and every package this
tree writes is far longer than its own table, so the check it weakens never fires on a
well-formed file.

Expected to fail: the harness's panic-freedom claim rather than either assertion, as an
out-of-bounds slice inside `extent`. A header claiming sixty-four members in a 272-byte buffer
passes the weakened length check and `parse` then indexes a table entry that is not there. This
is the install path, so the buffer is whatever arrived.

diff --git a/crates/package_archive/src/lib.rs b/crates/package_archive/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/package_archive/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/package_archive/src/lib.rs
@@ -250,3 +250,3 @@ impl<'a> Package<'a> {
         }
-        let table_end = HEADER_LEN + count * MEMBER_LEN;
+        let table_end = HEADER_LEN + count;
